		<item>
			<title>The problem with calling models open or closed</title>
			<link>https://chenyangsu.github.io/blog/the-problem-with-calling-models-open-or-closed/</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="true">https://chenyangsu.github.io/blog/the-problem-with-calling-models-open-or-closed/</guid>
			<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:12:40 +0000</pubDate>
			<category>artificial intelligence</category>
			<category>open weights</category>
			<category>AI safety</category>
			<category>AI regulation</category>
			<category>open science</category>
			<description>A safety argument and a commercial interest can point the same way, and from the outside they look identical. Human genetics has spent decades drawing this line; the lesson is to regulate what a system can do, not how it is distributed.</description>
		</item>

